<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The light a deathresting pilot's warcasket casts: an unseen thing on the pilot's cell
    whose glower is on the map's glow grid for as long as it stands there
    (Source/1.6/Rendering/DeathrestLight.cs, spawned by DeathrestGlow). The rush has no such
    light: a glower that moved with a running pilot would have the glow grid rebuilt around
    it step by step, where a deathrester lies still and costs it one change as the light
    comes on and one as it goes.

    Glower: glowRadius 1.9 reaches the eight cells around the pilot and no further, under
    the smallest of the game's own glowers at 2. glowColor is the glow sprites' red
    (1, 0.2, 0.15) at under half strength, a dim wash. It is real light all the same: the
    game counts a cell as lit from a strongest channel of 22, so the pilot's cell and its
    neighbors stop being dark for mood and work speed.

    Shape: category Ethereal as the game's own unseen things are (Core's
    Ethereal_Various.xml), which blocks and wipes nothing. A Mote would stay out of the
    mouseover readout but carries no thing id, which the glow grid finds a glower by, so
    this is listed there and takes a label for it. tickerType Rare is the thing's own check
    that its pilot is still deathresting on its cell. isSaveable false keeps it out of
    saves: DeathrestGlow puts it back within a second of a load.
  -->
  <ThingDef>
    <defName>HPWC_DeathrestLight</defName>
    <label>hemogen glow</label>
    <thingClass>HemophageWarcasket.DeathrestLight</thingClass>
    <category>Ethereal</category>
    <tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
    <drawerType>None</drawerType>
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <selectable>false</selectable>
    <isSaveable>false</isSaveable>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Glower">
        <glowRadius>1.9</glowRadius>
        <glowColor>(120, 24, 18, 0)</glowColor>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>
</Defs>
